ITEMS = ((('what should i do when someone has a seizure', 'how do i help a person having a seizure', 'what is the first aid for seizures', 'how to respond to a seizure', 'what to do during a fit during a seizure', 'how do you handle seizures', 'what helps during a seizure episode', 'how can i assist with seizures', 'what is the best response to a seizure', 'how should i care for someone having a seizure'), 'During a seizure, keep the person safe from injury, loosen tight clothing and do not hold them down. Time the fit and stay with them. Call emergency services if it lasts a long time, repeats, or the person does not recover.'), (('should i put anything in the mouth during a seizure', 'can a person swallow their tongue during a seizure', 'what not to do during a seizure with seizures', 'should i hold someone down during a fit during a seizure', 'can i give water during a seizure', 'is it safe to move a person having a fit during a seizure', 'what if i panic during a seizure', 'how to protect the head during a seizure', 'should i shake someone awake during a seizure', 'who can advise on seizure safety'), 'Never put anything in the mouth or hold a person down during a seizure. Clear nearby hazards and cushion the head. Call emergency services if the fit is prolonged or the person is injured.'), (('how long is too long for a seizure', 'when should an ambulance be called for a seizure', 'what if a fit does not stop during a seizure', 'how to time a seizure', 'what if seizures happen again', 'is a brief seizure an emergency', 'what to tell the operator about a fit during a seizure', 'when to seek help after a first seizure', 'what if the person is confused afterwards during a seizure', 'who can assess prolonged seizures'), 'Call emergency services if a seizure lasts longer than usual, seems prolonged, or another starts soon after. A first seizure, injury or breathing difficulty also needs urgent assessment. Tell the operator how long it lasted.'), (('what to do after a seizure ends', 'how to place someone after a fit during a seizure', 'what if the person is drowsy after a seizure', 'how to check breathing after seizures', 'should i give food after a seizure', 'how to comfort someone after a fit during a seizure', 'what if they are confused during a seizure', 'how long to stay with someone during a seizure', 'when to call a doctor after a seizure', 'who should review after a fit during a seizure'), 'After a seizure, check breathing and place the person in the recovery position if drowsy. Stay with them and speak calmly. Do not give food or drink until fully alert, and ask a doctor to assess a first or unusual fit.'), (('what causes seizures', 'can fever cause seizures in children', 'what if a seizure follows a head injury', 'can low blood sugar cause a fit during a seizure', 'what medical conditions lead to seizures', 'can stress trigger a seizure', 'what if there is no known condition during a seizure', 'how to find out the cause during a seizure', 'when to ask a doctor about causes during a seizure', 'who can investigate seizures'), 'Seizures can be linked to epilepsy, fever in children, head injury, low blood sugar or other illness. You do not need the cause to give first aid. A doctor should investigate a first episode or a change in usual fits.'), (('how do i help a child with a seizure', 'what to do for a baby having a fit during a seizure', 'are childhood seizures different', 'how to protect a child during a fit during a seizure', "when to call help for a child's seizure", 'what if a child turns blue during a seizure', 'how to time a fit in a child during a seizure', 'how to place a child after a seizure', 'what to tell the operator during a seizure', 'who can assess a child after a fit during a seizure'), 'For a child having a seizure, move hazards away and time the fit. Call emergency services if it is prolonged, the child turns blue or seems unwell afterwards. Keep them warm and place them on their side when the fit ends.'), (('what if someone has seizures in water', 'can a seizure lead to drowning', 'how to help a person fitting near water during a seizure', 'what if a swimmer has a fit during a seizure', 'should i support the head in water during a seizure', 'how to get help at a pool during a seizure', 'what to do after bringing them out during a seizure', 'when to call emergency services during a seizure', 'how to watch breathing after a seizure in water', 'who can advise about water safety during a seizure'), 'A seizure in water can quickly lead to drowning. Call emergency services, get the person to safety if you can do so safely, and check breathing. Place them on their side and keep them warm until help arrives.'), (('what is status epilepticus during a seizure', 'why is a long seizure dangerous', 'how to recognise an emergency seizure', 'what if a seizure will not stop', 'how long can a fit safely last during a seizure', 'what to do while waiting for help during a seizure', 'should i use rescue medicine during a seizure', 'what if the person stops breathing during a seizure', 'how to hand over to paramedics during a seizure', 'who can treat a prolonged seizure'), 'A seizure that continues or repeats without recovery is a medical emergency. Call emergency services, protect the person from injury and time the fit. If they have prescribed rescue medicine, help them use it as directed.'), (('how can i support someone with epilepsy during a seizure', "what to know about a person's seizure plan", 'should i ask about triggers during a seizure', 'how to record a seizure', 'what if seizures are frequent', 'how to plan travel with epilepsy during a seizure', 'when to discuss treatment changes during a seizure', 'what if medication is missed during a seizure', 'who can review epilepsy care during a seizure', 'how to reduce injury risk during a seizure'), 'Ask the person what helps and follow any seizure plan they have. Keep a simple record of timing and features to share with their doctor. Ask a healthcare professional about treatment if seizures are frequent or changing.'), (('what symptoms after a seizure need urgent help', 'should i call if the person will not wake during a seizure', 'what if breathing is noisy after a fit during a seizure', 'how to check for injury after a seizure', 'what if the person seems confused for a long time during a seizure', 'when to seek help twice during a seizure', 'what if a seizure happens in public', 'how to keep bystanders calm during a seizure', 'what to report to the crew during a seizure', 'who can decide about hospital care during a seizure'), 'Get urgent help if the person does not wake, has noisy breathing, seems injured or the confusion lasts. Call emergency services if you are worried. Tell the crew about the timing and what happened before and after the fit.'))
